  "description": "NaAgO crystallizes in the tetragonal I4/mmm space group. Na¹⁺ is bonded in a see-saw-like geometry to four equivalent O²⁻ atoms. There are two shorter (2.31 Å) and two longer (2.33 Å) Na-O bond lengths. Ag¹⁺ is bonded in a linear geometry to two equivalent O²⁻ atoms. Both Ag-O bond lengths are 2.07 Å. O²⁻ is bonded to four equivalent Na¹⁺ and two equivalent Ag¹⁺ atoms to form a mixture of corner and edge-sharing ONa₄Ag₂ octahedra. The corner-sharing octahedral tilt angles range from 2-14°.",
